      <Output>
        <ErrorInfo>
          <Message>a JWT validator wrote its own ClockSkew instead of using JwtValidationDefaults.ClockSkew — that is BL-296 coming back: the same token judged differently by two services, 30 seconds wide and invisible from the symptom. Use the shared constant; if the value itself is wrong, change it in services/Diten.Building.Blocks/Diten.BuildingBlocks.Security.Secrets/JwtValidationDefaults.cs so every service moves together:
services/Diten.HumanCapitalService/src/Diten.HumanCapitalService.Api/Program.cs
services/Diten.TalentEcosystemService/src/Diten.TalentEcosystemService.Api/Program.cs</Message>
          <StackTrace>   at TenantArchitecture.ArchitectureTests.JwtClockSkewGuardTests.NoProductionValidatorWritesItsOwnClockSkew() in /Users/natig/Projects/ERP-vNext-recovery/tests/architecture/TenantArchitecture.ArchitectureTests/JwtClockSkewGuardTests.cs:line 76
